From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6afe-dai: TDM bit clock attribute from the DT

The TDM bit clocks are always set up inverted
(Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ATTRIBUTE_INVERT_COUPLE_NO). Not every board wants
that: the Galaxy Z Flip3's CS35L41 amps sample on the inverted edge
themselves (DSP_A, IB_NF, as downstream sets them), and downstream's
qcom,msm-cpudai-tdm-clk-attribute keeps the AFE clock as it is (1). With
both inverting, the amps sampled on the edge the AFE launches data on
and the speakers played loud noise.

Add an optional qcom,tdm-clk-attribute to the TDM ports; without it the
clock stays inverted, as before.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../bindings/sound/qcom,q6dsp-lpass-ports.yaml     |   11 +++++++++++
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c                   |    6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+)


diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,q6dsp-lpass-ports.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,q6dsp-lpass-ports.yaml
index 3b03e2a..a17799c 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,q6dsp-lpass-ports.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,q6dsp-lpass-ports.yaml
@@ -100,6 +100,17 @@ patternProperties:
             0 = MSB
             1 = LSB
 
+      qcom,tdm-clk-attribute:
+        $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+        enum: [1, 2, 3, 4]
+        description:
+          Attribute of the TDM bit clock the DSP generates. When absent the
+          clock is inverted (4).
+            1 = not coupled
+            2 = coupled, dividend
+            3 = coupled, divisor
+            4 = inverted, not coupled
+
     required:
       - reg
 
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c
index bafa174..cb8af9a 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ struct q6afe_dai_priv_data {
 	uint32_t invert_sync;
 	uint32_t data_delay;
 	uint32_t data_align;
+	uint32_t clk_attribute;	/* TDM bit clock, Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ATTRIBUTE_* */
 };
 
 struct q6afe_dai_data {
@@ -513,7 +514,9 @@ static int q6afe_mi2s_set_sysclk(struct snd_soc_dai *dai,
 					     Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ROOT_DEFAULT,
 					     freq, dir);
 	case Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ID_PRI_TDM_IBIT ... Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ID_QUIN_TDM_EBIT:
+		/* inverted unless the port says otherwise (qcom,tdm-clk-attribute) */
 		return q6afe_port_set_sysclk(port, clk_id,
+					     dai_data->priv[dai->id].clk_attribute ?:
 					     Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ATTRIBUTE_INVERT_COUPLE_NO,
 					     Q6AFE_LPASS_CLK_ROOT_DEFAULT,
 					     freq, dir);
@@ -1150,6 +1153,9 @@ static void of_q6afe_parse_dai_data(struct device *dev,
 				dev_err(dev, "No Data align from DT\n");
 				break;
 			}
+			/* optional: the bit clock attribute, inverted by default */
+			of_property_read_u32(node, "qcom,tdm-clk-attribute",
+					     &priv->clk_attribute);
 			break;
 		default:
 			break;
